{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then encode the exploration/recovery policy in deterministic specifications. Clear sensing leads primarily to random_walk, with a separate short forward-progress state reached after path_clear from recovery. Obstacle events always enter dedicated recovery states with exactly one safe action, and action states self-loop on path_clear so intended one-shot pulses are not preempted.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation into plant automata, and place the task policy in specification automata.",
    "Use one-shot commit/recovery states: clear exploration uses random_walk, path_clear after recovery enables move_forward, obstacle_left prefers rotate_clockwise, obstacle_right prefers rotate_counterclockwise, and obstacle_front first uses move_backward."
  ],
